  "rules": "All 16 I.2 universal substitutions over A/B and u/v; all 12 incidence equality transports over A/B/C and u/v. No target-conditioned block or cone. Closed object names are constants, not coordinates.",
  "grammar": "Fixed 4 or 3 proof rows. Original axiom/refl/tautology/MP command forms over 27 declared interfaces; no generalization because variables are empty. All block/output pairs and every strict-earlier input pair included. C/G/I1/I2 roots all generation zero; compact injective scalar catalog markings.",
  "scope": "Symbolic guarded Hilbert I.2 incidence uniqueness plus equality. The extra point C is named by a constant and has an incidence hypothesis; no Point(C) hypothesis is needed for equality substitution. Full Hilbert geometry, existential witnesses, classic intersection theorem, and universality remain unfinished.",
  "controls": "Omitting I.2 changes theory and rule inventory. Three rows changes boundary. Both are scope controls, not equivalent acceleration baselines. Repetitions repeat frozen deterministic counts and measure timing, not generalization statistics.",
